      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the product rule for logarithms, combine the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(5\\right)+\\ln\\left(x\\right)-\\ln\\left(z\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(5\\cdot x\\right)-\\ln\\left(z\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow use the quotient rule to combine the remaining difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\ln\\left(5\\cdot x\\right)-\\ln\\left(z\\right) \\\\ &=\\ln\\left(\\frac{5\\cdot x}{z}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
